cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it together with the archived dataset listed under identifiers."
type: software

title: "TRPL/SSPL Multitrap Analysis"
abstract: >-
  Two complementary Python toolsets for extracting trap parameters from
  time-resolved (TRPL) and steady-state (SSPL) photoluminescence measurements
  of semiconductor thin films using Shockley–Read–Hall recombination models.
  Provides CMA-ES parameter fitting with an optional neural-network surrogate
  for the transient solver, and a Bayesian grid pipeline that maps the posterior
  over the full parameter space and reports credible intervals.

